TEXT 0 -448 Left 2 ;Problems 7.4 - 315 SWR on an infinite baffle (Leach, lecture 7 slide 27).  IMPEDANCE analogy in all three domains:
TEXT 0 -416 Left 2 ;electrical V = voltage, I = current  |  mechanical V = force, I = velocity  |  acoustical V = pressure, I = volume velocity
TEXT 0 -368 Left 2 !.param Re=5.46 Bl=11.6 Mmd=0.074629 Rms=3.25 Cms=0.00055 Sd=0.051854
TEXT 0 -336 Left 2 !.param MA1=2.5237 RA1=3510.7 RA2=7960.9 CA1=8.8702e-08
TEXT 0 352 Left 2 ;acoustic load: front + back face, each a baffled piston (Z_AF = Z_AB = Z_ar), drawn as ONE network with every element doubled
TEXT 0 384 Left 2 ;V(pD) = p_F + p_B = 2 Z_ar U drives the reaction force;  near-field (front) pressure p_near = V(pD)/2
TEXT 1344 304 Left 2 ;outputs for e_g = 1 V (plot in dB: V(SPLff), V(SPLnf) read directly as dB SPL)
TEXT 0 880 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 5 20k
TEXT 0 928 Left 2 ;far field (1 m) p = j*w*rho/(2*pi*r) * Sd*u  -> E_ff = rho*Sd/(2 pi r 20u) * s.   Z_E = V(eg)/I(Vd1).   displacement: V(xD) [m per V]
TEXT 0 960 Left 2 ;check: |Z_E| peaks at f_s = 22.9 Hz with R_E + Bl^2/R_MS = 46.9 ohm;  mid-band V(SPLff) = 81.5 dB (sensitivity -12.4 dB re 1 Pa/V)
